#         Security headers (Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build
#         output directory). GitHub Pages cannot set response headers at all,
#         which is one of the reasons for moving.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy below is only writable because the app now loads
# zero third-party assets and has no inline <script> or inline event handlers:
# script-src can therefore be 'self' with no escape hatches, which is the
# directive that actually stops cross-site scripting. This app renders a lot of
# user-supplied text (manager names, chat messages, league names) through
# innerHTML; it escapes that text, but CSP is what turns a single missed escape
# from a stolen-account bug into a blocked console error.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https://media.api-sports.io https://*.incrowdsports.com data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://gpdyemrgulhdnsmmadgs.supabase.co wss://gpdyemrgulhdnsmmadgs.supabase.co https://v3.football.api-sports.io; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

# Long-lived, content-addressed assets. app.js and styles.css are rebuilt on
# every deploy, so revalidate them rather than caching hard.
/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# On the image hosts:
#   media.api-sports.io    — football player photos and club crests.
#   *.incrowdsports.com    — the rugby feed's own domain, which is where it
#     serves club crests and player photos from. A wildcard over the vendor we
#     already trust for the data itself, rather than a guessed subdomain: the
#     feed hands out absolute URLs and does not promise which host they sit on.
#     If a crest is ever refused, the console names the host it wanted and the
#     app falls back to the club's three-letter code rather than breaking.
#
# Notes on the two deliberate relaxations:
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'  — the app sets style attributes (the matchday
#     ticker duration, the header rule). Inline *style* cannot execute script,
#     so this is a much smaller concession than inline script would be.
#   COOP same-origin-allow-popups — required for the Google sign-in popup flow.
